Backport the unreleased upstream master code onto the v0.6.1 tarball.

Upstream jsh58/Genrich has published no release since v0.6.1 (2021-03-17), but
its master branch has moved on. This patch carries the commits that follow the
v0.6.1 tag up to da439890cfcbf8feaff473e8e703dceae2d385c0 (2023-05-08), the
current tip of upstream master.

Two user-visible changes:

  1. FEATURE -- a new `-L <int>` option that overrides the genome length Genrich
     otherwise derives from the SAM/BAM header (the @SQ length sum, minus any
     -E excluded regions). The value feeds the background lambda, and hence the
     pileup significance and q-value calculations. It is accepted both in a
     normal run and when calling peaks from a log file (-P). Upstream commits
     b736b8a, 076c083 and 8ce0521.

  2. BUG FIX -- checkHeader() dereferenced the @HD SO: value while stripping its
     trailing newline, before testing whether an SO: field was present at all.
     SO is optional in @HD under the SAM specification, so a spec-valid header
     carrying only VN: segfaulted Genrich, regardless of -S. The trim is now
     guarded, and the existing `order == NULL` test -- previously unreachable
     for that case -- handles the missing sort order as intended. Upstream
     commit da43989.

Also included: the README documentation for -L, and an upstream fix to a dead
`awk` reference link (commit 368ff7a).

DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED -- the VERSION string bump to "0.6.2" that upstream made
in 8ce0521. This recipe still builds the v0.6.1 tarball and is versioned 0.6.1,
so the binary is left self-reporting 0.6.1 rather than shipping a package whose
`Genrich -V` output contradicts its conda version. VERSION is referenced exactly
once in the whole codebase -- the "Genrich, version %s" line in Genrich.c -- so
holding it back has no functional effect whatsoever.

Everything else in the range is applied verbatim: after this patch the tree is
identical to upstream master apart from those two lines. The v0.6.1 and master
trees contain the same set of files, and Makefile, LICENSE, findNs.py and
figures/ are byte-identical between them, so nothing outside Genrich.c,
Genrich.h and README.md needs carrying.
